From 920048717308893182d1e564ef2bd26a89e172f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ricardo Akinaga <245769618+ricardoakinaga-dev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 23:30:21 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] AUD0621 SPEC0248: bound decision budget, cancellation and
 response receipt

Implements SPEC0248 r3 (sha256 d4392f0b) for AUD-0621 findings F02, F03,
F04, F13, F14 and the core part of F21.

- harness: the iterative decision reserves every decision model call and
  repair through a runtime-owned budget port that uses the kernel's
  beginModelRequest/recordModelResult; reported usage is copied and
  validated before it is counted and is kept on orchestrator failure; the
  context build and the decision race the absolute deadline and the
  caller's cancellation; a cancellation is re-checked right before dispatch.
- orchestrator: HybridOrchestrator asks the optional DecisionModelGate
  before each call and repair; OrchestratorDecisionError carries usage and
  the new budget_exhausted code. The shared contracts are unchanged.
- model-gateway: an aborted signal reserves nothing and reaches no
  provider; the backoff races the signal; request and profile maxCostUsd
  deny a non-finite or over-ceiling estimate before any reservation; the
  bound transport cuts a body at the ceiling with HTTP status priority
  (SPEC0180 D011 subset); providers read bodies under the ceiling.
- channel-gateway: Evolution and Chatwoot send with a deadline (DNS to end
  of body, 20 s default) and pass the byte ceiling to the transport.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
